From: Gleb Pesin <dormancygrace@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] vi: hand back the tuning buffers on every setup

vi_tuning_buf_setup() runs on every vi_start_streaming() and on
VI_IOCTL_GET_TUN_ADDR. The pool is allocated once and never cleared
(vi_tuning_mempool_clear() is commented out in setup), so the second run,
for example capture restarted while the input size is detected at boot,
logged "tuning_buf pool already allocated" at error level and returned
without filling the pointers. The callers kept the first pointers in
static variables, so nothing broke, but every boot showed a kernel error.

The pool has a fixed layout: return the same buffers every time.
---
--- a/interdrv/vi/chip/cv181x/vip/vi_tun_ip_ctrl.c
+++ b/interdrv/vi/chip/cv181x/vip/vi_tun_ip_ctrl.c
@@ -271,11 +271,10 @@
 	u32 offset_be = VI_ALIGN(sizeof(struct cvi_vip_isp_post_cfg));
 	u32 offset_fe = offset_be + VI_ALIGN(sizeof(struct cvi_vip_isp_be_cfg));
 
-	if (tuning_buf_pool[raw_num].is_allocated) {
-		vi_pr(VI_ERR, "tuning_buf pool already allocated\n");
-		return;
-	}
-
+	/*
+	 * The pool has a fixed layout, so a second call (streaming restarted,
+	 * or VI_IOCTL_GET_TUN_ADDR after start) gets the same buffers back.
+	 */
 	*post_cfg = (struct cvi_vip_isp_post_cfg*)(tuning_buf_pool[raw_num].memory + offset_post);
 	*be_cfg = (struct cvi_vip_isp_be_cfg*)(tuning_buf_pool[raw_num].memory + offset_be);
 	*fe_cfg = (struct cvi_vip_isp_fe_cfg*)(tuning_buf_pool[raw_num].memory + offset_fe);
